# /sdd-context

Purpose:
  Compile, inspect, and validate context packs for tasks.

Owns: commands/sdd-context.sdd

Description:
  Reads task definition, resolves intent, runs Context Compiler,
  and produces minimal context pack for AI execution.

Usage:
  /sdd-context --task T<id>
  /sdd-context --intent "<text>"
  /sdd-context --compile
  /sdd-context --manifest C<id>
  /sdd-context --validate C<id>
  /sdd-context --budget <LOW|MEDIUM|HIGH|CRITICAL>
  /sdd-context --explain C<id>

Options:
  --task       Compile context for specific task
  --intent     Compile context from natural language intent
  --compile    Force recompilation
  --manifest   Show manifest for existing context pack
  --validate   Check context health (broken refs, contradictions, staleness)
  --budget     Override risk-based budget
  --explain    Show why references were included/excluded

Mode: READ_ONLY

Output:
  CONTEXT PACK

    Task:           T2041
    Layers:         L0, L1, L2, L4, L6
    References:     17
    Budget:         40 refs / 16k tokens
    Confidence:     HIGH
    Freshness:      FRESH
    Contradictions: 1

    Included:
      [L1] @task.T2041
      [L2] @project.P01
      [L4] @skill.repository
      [L4] @skill.transaction
      [L6] @decision.D21

    Excluded:
      @skill.frontend: outside_task_scope
      @analytics.*:    outside_task_scope

    Contradictions:
      D12 (REST) vs D41 (GraphQL for payments)

ContextCompilation (adopted 2026-09-14, external research RA-1/RA-2;
source: .sdd/docs/analysis/external-research-2026-09.md):
  dependsOnTraversal: when compiling a pack for a task/change, the
    compiler walks the .sdd dependencies graph TRANSITIVELY from
    every spec the change touches — what the spec graph itself
    declares relevant is included, not only what the task names.
  stalenessFallback: each included item carries freshness metadata
    (git last-commit vs declared); a STALE item is injected with its
    RAW content plus a staleness notice — never silently trusted
    stale structured metadata.
  rationale: compiled context vs agent-discovered context measured
    5-6x token reduction (Moderne 2026-04); structural retrieval
    precision@5 0.140 -> 0.478 (Sourcegraph); SpecD resolves context
    for the agent — same doctrine as EXPAND ([CMD7]).

Rules:
  [CTX-CMD-01] /sdd-context MUST produce manifest for every compilation.
  [CTX-CMD-02] /sdd-context MUST flag contradictions.
  [CTX-CMD-03] /sdd-context MUST respect budget.
  [CTX-CMD-04] /sdd-context MUST show exclusion reasons.
  [CTX-CMD-05] Compilation MUST traverse declared spec dependencies
                transitively from touched specs (dependsOnTraversal).
  [CTX-CMD-06] Stale items MUST fall back to raw content + staleness
                notice; stale structured metadata is never injected
                silently (stalenessFallback).

